<title>FRANCE: French June trade surplus 9.75 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French June trade surplus 9.75 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>France had a seasonally adjusted trade surplus in June of 9.75 billion francs compared with a revised surplus in May of 11.24 billion, provisional customs office data showed on Friday.</p>
<p>The office had originally reported a surplus in May of 11.59 billion francs.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures, in billions of francs and seasonally adjusted unless otherwise stated, were as follows:</p>
<p>					  June     May</p>
<p> Trade balance			 9.75   11.24</p>
<p> Trade balance (unadjusted)     11.15    9.61</p>
<p> Imports			     107.39  111.62</p>
<p> Exports			     117.14  122.86</p>
<p> Agri-business balance	     3.28    4.62</p>
<p> Energy balance		     -5.94   -6.00</p>
<p> Industrial/military balance     8.48    8.55</p>
<p> Airbus exports	 4.47 (11 planes)  3.70 (9)</p>
<p> Defence (unadj)		     0.62    1.47</p>
<p> Unadjusted exports		123.11  120.96</p>
<p> Unadjusted imports		111.97  111.35</p>
<p> European Union			2.74    4.10</p>
<p> Germany				 0.38    1.02</p>
<p> Japan				  -1.02   -0.83</p>
<p> United States			-0.86   -1.25</p>
<p>Cumulative figures for the first six months of the year were as follows</p>
<p>				     Jan-Jun 1996     Jan-Jun 1995</p>
<p> Before seasonal adjustment    56.43		53.41</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted	     53.28		52.90</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5381</p>
</text>
